    "body": "## Problem\n\nui2 positions the msg window with `:normal! Gzb`, and `:normal` sets `v:count`. When a mapping with a count prints a message, the msg_show handler runs in the middle of the mapping, so `v:count` is 0 for the rest of it.\n\n## Solution\n\nSave and restore `v:count`, `v:count1` and `v:prevcount` around `vim.ui_attach()` handlers, the same way `ui_call_event()` already handles textlock. This keeps the `:normal` that ui2 needs and fixes the problem for any other handler that does the same.\n\nFixes #42292\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-31T17:01:02Z",
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42607#discussion_r4432526678"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/42607"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/4432526678"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This fixes a random symptom without any real thought. There is unlimited global state that can be changed in a handler. And there are lots of other handlers besides ui-attach handlers. So why are we randomly save/restoring this here?",
            "commit_id": "8d1a57b33425b221652d1ffd00ff5d0d16111225",
            "copilot_code_review_sources": [],
            "created_at": "2026-10-31T17:00:52Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -794,6 +795,10 @@ void ui_call_event(char *name, Array args)\n   int save_textlock = textlock;\n   expr_map_lock = 0;\n   textlock = 0;\n+  // Don't let UI event handlers reset v:count, e.g. with :normal.\n+  varnumber_T save_prevcount = get_vim_var_nr(VV_PREVCOUNT);\n+  varnumber_T save_count = get_vim_var_nr(VV_COUNT);\n+  varnumber_T save_count1 = get_vim_var_nr(VV_COUNT1);",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42607#discussion_r4432526678",
